00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
vision is a classic marvel character now  known to millions as part of the mcu  from his humble roots in the comics to  his unique story on screen this is  everything you don't know about the  mysterious android  vision may be the most popular character  with that name in the marvel universe  but he wasn't the first to claim the  moniker  decades before the vision you know first  appeared a totally different character  named vision appeared in 1940's marvel  mystery comics number 13.  also operating under the name arcus this  vision is an alien who has teleportation  and ice based superpowers  he occasionally fights alongside  superheroes like the human torch and  namor as part of the invaders an early  marvel superhero team  in the 1960s a number of these classic  golden age characters including captain  america and neymar came back into the  spotlight vision however  was not lucky enough to receive this  treatment though comics writer roy ryder  initially wanted to revive arcus for the  1960s  company mandates forced him to create a  new character for the name vision to be  applied to instead  thus the very first vision in marvel  comics history quickly faded into  obscurity however that doesn't mean this  early vision has been totally forgotten  since the 1970s arcus has managed to  make a handful of appearances in the  comics  including the 2013 x-men legacy story  line  most recently he managed to become a  playable character in the mobile video  game marvel contest of champions  some superheroes like to dress  exclusively in bleak colors  not so for vision this particular  avenger is readily identifiable by his  head to toe bold colors  a yellow cape and gloves complement  vision's green body and red face  he's easy to spot in any crowd however  his distinct look wasn't popular with  one very important person at marvel  creator roy thomas explained to the  hollywood reporter stanley hated the  color of the vision  why'd you make him red red's not a good  color i didn't want to make him green  like the hulk or blue like the  atlanteans i suppose i could have made  him white but the paper we printed on  was so poor that you would have been  able to see the other side so we didn't  make things white that we didn't have to  though stan lee wasn't initially  satisfied with vision's colors it's  those same hues that have made him one  of the most visually distinctive marvel  superheroes around  sometimes iconic characters come about  due to spur the moment creative  inspiration  others like vision come out of something  as simple as a mandate from a boss  according to roy thomas vision was  created as a solution to stan lee's  mandate for new avengers members  thomas explained to yahoo stan suddenly  said it was time to make up a new  character to bring in a new avenger  i didn't like to create new characters  for marvel because i wouldn't own  them i wanted to bring back the old  vision but stan wanted an android  he didn't say why he just said he wanted  the new character to be an android  thus the vision the world knows and  loves was born all thanks to stan lee's  insistence on an android adventure  it may not be the glossiest origin story  for an iconic superhero but lee's  mandate did have its advantages  chiefly it immediately helped make  vision stand out on any avengers roster  and still does in fact  the distinguished superhero team is at  all kinds of unusual members but an  android like vision still manages to  catch your attention all these years  later  in the 50 plus years he's existed vision  has often drawn comparisons to star trek  spock  it isn't hard to see why on the surface  there is the fact that they're both  sci-fi characters introduced in the late  1960s  on a deeper more specific level they're  both no-nonsense figures who are usually  the only non-humanoid members of their  group  what does thomas say about these  comparisons he told yahoo people have  told me they see a resemblance to mr  spock  if there is i didn't do it consciously i  was vaguely aware of the show  we would play poker while our wives and  kids sat in the next room watching star  trek so i would hear the tv playing  rather than using spock as a model  thomas actually drew inspiration from a  robot named adam link and otto bender's  short story irobot  in this tale which also inspired isaac  asimov's book of the same name  link is falsely accused of murdering his  creator in the ensuing chaos link  becomes all too aware of the adverse  effects his very existence has on human  beings who are immediately suspicious of  a robot  adam link's tragically self-conscious  qualities are immediately apparent in  vision in addition to the character's  unintentional overlap with mr spock  in the marvel cinematic universe vision  is played by actor paul bettany  prior to his multi-film turn his vision  betany appeared in a wide variety of  movies  among those acting credits was an  earlier role in the mcu as tony stark's  ai helper jarvis  jarvis you there that's your service a  reimagining to the comics edwin jarvis  who is a human butler jarvis was not a  role that bettany initially put much  stock in  at the time of iron man's release betany  said that while he was recording his  voice work for jarvis he didn't actually  know that it was for a superhero movie  while betany started out as an outsider  oblivious to the larger machinations of  the marvel cinematic universe he didn't  remain that way for long  after playing jarvis across four  different mcu installments it was  announced in february 2014 that betany  would be taken on a physical role in the  mcu's vision  when joss whedon was putting together  his ideas for avengers age of ultron  he intended to use the mammoth box  office success of the original avengers  to realize some of his grander ambitions  specifically he wanted to use ultron as  the primary villain and introduced  vision as played by paul bettany  like many of whedon's plans for age of  ultron this was a notion he had carried  with him long before the cameras even  started rolling on the first avengers  movie he told collider  before i took the first avengers i said  well i don't know if i'm right for this  or if i want it or you want me  but in the second one the villain has to  be ultron and he has to create the  vision  and then that has to be paul bettany  whedon went on to note that his  fascination with the character derives  from vision's unusual power set  as well as the fact that vision was a  focal point to the comics he grew up  reading  as for his long-standing dream of having  bethany inhabit the role the director  joked that betany's sharp cheekbones  make him a natural fit for the part  though he's existed for over half a  century in the marvel comics canon  vision has usually acted as a supporting  player first introduced in the comics as  a creation of ultron who was convinced  to fight back against his creator vision  subsequently became a fixture of the  avengers comic books  over the years vision is factored  prominently into the avengers adventures  the wedding between himself and scarlet  witch even acts as the centerpiece of  giant size avengers number four  still being a standout member of an  ensemble is not the same thing as  headlining your own comic series a feat  that most other marvel superheroes have  been able to do regularly  while vision has been a supporting  player for most of his fictional life he  still played a major role in numerous  story lines that have shaped the marvel  universe moreover the characters managed  to secure a handful of solo adventures  over the years  the first of these was a four-issue  vision series published in 1994 by bob  harris and manny clark  more recent his 2015's 12 issue vision  series by tom king and gabriel hernandez  walter  even if vision isn't a go-to figure for  headlining marvel comic books  these acclaimed stories starring the  mysterious character show the value  vision has  as a leading man if you're going to be a  superhero in the marvel cinematic  universe you're gonna have to put on an  elaborate costume sometimes this costume  is the motion capture suit mark ruffalo  has to wear to portray the hulk  other times it's a patriotic getup chris  evans had to pull on to captain america  in the case of paul bettany properly  portraying vision means having to  undergo extensive application of makeup  and prosthetics  transforming betany into the boldly  colored vision is not an easy task  a two-hour process is required to make  the man into the machine perfecting  vision's look proved to be a  time-consuming task even in the concept  stage  well before paul bettany took his seat  in the makeup chair the makeup artists  for avengers age of ultron were so  determined to get the character's unique  look right that they put extraordinary  effort into mocking up some prototypes  for the final product  makeup artist nick williams told makeup  artist magazine in 2015  the makeup went through a lot of stages  in order to make the lines absolutely  perfect as though he was born from a  computer we actually sculpted the makeup  in 3d  over a cyber scan of paul's head and  printed out in clear plastic  while vision's look wasn't easy to put  together all this exacting effort  certainly paid off  vision came to the silver screen looking  like he'd walk straight out of a comic  book  vision isn't the first character to  carry that moniker in the comics so it  should be no surprise that he's also not  the last character to bear that name  either whereas the vision created in  1967  is a massive departure from the one  created in the 1940s though the newest  superheroes to carry on the vision name  have been directly inspired by the  crimson colored android  in 2005 a new version of vision debuted  in young avengers number 5. while he  looks like a dead ringer for the  original vision this new hero is younger  and goes by the name jonas  speaking of newer and younger versions  of vision the mainstream vision's most  notable superhero successor emerged in  the form of his own daughter vibvision  first appearing in vision number one the  character starts out as one part of  vision's fragmented attempt to create a  traditional american nuclear family for  himself  in the years since that run viv is  blossomed into a standalone superhero in  her own right  in a 2018 interview betany revealed that  the chance to portray vision in the  marvel cinematic universe came just as  it looked like his acting opportunities  were about to dry up  i had just had a meeting with a producer  who will remain  nameless who told me that my career was  over  for a short time after that meeting the  actor was gripped with despair before  getting a phone call from age of ultron  director joss whedon whedon proceeded to  ask if betany wanted to play vision in  the then  upcoming avengers sequel now one phone  call turned things around for bethany  completely as betany reflected to  insider i sort of looked up to heaven  and thought karma's very quick these  days  it happened just like that i sat down  and my phone rang very funny but you  know if i had a dollar for every time  somebody told me my career was over  my career could be over since then  betany has portrayed vision in a number  of mcu titles and the franchise's first  disney plus series won division  beyond the mcu betany has also landed  roles in films like solo a star wars  story and uncle frank  so whoever it was who said bethany's  career was over just moments before he  landed one of the biggest roles of his  career  probably needs to have their own vision  checked check out one of our newest  videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite comics characters are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

